From: NeoDarwin
Subject: [PATCH] sleh: acknowledge and complete Group 0 interrupts on generic GICv3

sleh_fiq reads ICC_IAR0_EL1 and writes ICC_EOIR0_EL1 only for
APPLEVIRTUALPLATFORM, the other board config with a GICv3. pe_fiq.c puts
the virtual timer (PPI 27) in Group 0 for SBSA as well, so the SBSA kernel
handled every timer FIQ without touching the GIC: the interrupt never
became active and was never completed. Timekeeping worked only because the
timer is level-sensitive, so reprogramming the deadline dropped the line
and the pending state with it. Found while tracing the IORTC boot stall
(no IAR0 reads in QEMU's GICv3 trace).

GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM now acknowledges and completes Group 0 as
APPLEVIRTUALPLATFORM does (EOImode 0, set by pe_fiq.c, so EOIR also
deactivates), as the bring-up design planned
(docs/kernel/arm64-sbsa-bringup.md §2.3).

Rebase-risk: low (two preprocessor conditions).
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c b/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c
--- a/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/sleh.c
@@ -2621,7 +2621,8 @@
 
 	sleh_interrupt_handler_prologue(state, type);
 
-#if APPLEVIRTUALPLATFORM
+#if APPLEVIRTUALPLATFORM || GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM
+	/* Group 0 (FIQ) is the GICv3 virtual timer, PPI 27 (pexpert/arm/pe_fiq.c). */
 	uint64_t iar = __builtin_arm_rsr64("ICC_IAR0_EL1");
 #endif
 
@@ -2667,7 +2668,7 @@
 		ml_interrupt_masked_debug_end();
 	}
 
-#if APPLEVIRTUALPLATFORM
+#if APPLEVIRTUALPLATFORM || GENERIC_ARM64_PLATFORM
 	if (iar != GIC_SPURIOUS_IRQ) {
 		__builtin_arm_wsr64("ICC_EOIR0_EL1", iar);
 		__builtin_arm_isb(ISB_SY);
